TITLE: REQ-VAL-002 · Reject division by zero

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VAL-002
VERSION: 1
TITLE: Reject division by zero
STATEMENT: >>>
If a division request has valid operands and a divisor `b` whose value is
zero, then the service **shall** reject the request with the error code
`DIVISION_BY_ZERO`.
<<<
KIND: functional
STATUS: draft
PRIORITY: high
SAFETY: QM
RELEASE: 1.0.0
VERIFICATION: test
VERIF_LEVELS: unit, system
TAGS: validation, division
SOURCE: Stakeholder request, 2026-11-18
OWNER: msforenter090
CREATED: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
RATIONALE: >>>
Division by zero has no result. A dedicated error code tells the client the
input was well formed but cannot be divided.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
- The value counts, not the spelling: `0`, `-0`, `+0`, `000` and `0.000`
  are all zero.
- If an operand is also invalid, `INVALID_NUMBER` (REQ-VAL-001) is
  returned instead.
<<<
